MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6439072644958447743}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 901c0ba4f64da4a15b6e582685b840f7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Arlen::Arlen.World.Waybell
  waybellId: waybell
  bell: {fileID: 174024684598245670}
  glowRenderers:
  - {fileID: 7449433185374132265}
  - {fileID: 3890806354368986136}
  - {fileID: 4958382032082950050}
  - {fileID: 8487312639343296791}
  - {fileID: 1486669327730054692}
  - {fileID: 4752396183151568229}
  - {fileID: 5797996379039882824}
  - {fileID: 765287584908789295}
  - {fileID: 1364605669275353428}
  - {fileID: 4042112562109942778}
  - {fileID: 2410693194136694404}
  - {fileID: 6267962430805776364}
  awakeEmission: {r: 0.35, g: 1.2, b: 1.1, a: 1}
  ring: {fileID: 5099878119460970230}
  ringRadius: 24
  resonators: []
  resonatorEmission: {r: 0.3, g: 1.4, b: 1.2, a: 1}
  chimeSeconds: 2.4
  awakeningLines:
  - You lay a paw on the cold bronze. For a heartbeat, nothing.
  - 'Then the Waybell sings: one deep note you feel in your bones more than hear.'
  - Light races through the runes beneath your feet. Somewhere to the west, the brambles on the old road shiver.
  - 'For an instant you see it clearly: the Mosswood Road, paved and whole, running north. Then the forest closes over it again.'
  - The bell knew you. Somehow, it knew you.
  listenLines:
  - The Waybell hums softly, warm to the touch, as if it is remembering something.
  - The road beyond the brambles is still lost. Whatever woke here is only the beginning.
